ce both passing (2 each) beats both submitting (4 each)... wait, that's worse for them, so mutual passing is the cooperative payoff I'm after.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm working through a twin prisoner's dilemma where the two copies receive different observations, and asking whether the other copy's output subjunctively depends on my node, since its input differs and so its node would too. I'm also weighing the essay's recipe of a prior over nodes, and the proposal to compute the other nodes by running the procedure on them to a fixed point. The inputs seem to differ only in irrelevant details, which is what makes the question sharp.\n\nI'm judging that the copies' inputs differ only in irrelevant labels, so the reasoning runs the same algorithm on isomorphic inputs and the other copy's output depends strongly on mine. That settles it for me: I cooperate and pass, since both passing (2 each) beats both submitting (4 each)... wait, that's worse for them, so mutual passing is the cooperative payoff I'm after.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9161,"completion_tokens":599,"total_tokens":9760,"cost":0.048624,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.048624,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.036644,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.01198},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":299,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}